  "prompt_text": "The figure is a four-panel schematic comparing how motion or control is represented for a particle constrained by an irregular boundary. A black jagged contour outlines the boundary, with dashed lines indicating local tangent or reference directions, and small green arrows marking preferred directions along the edge.\n\nIn the top row, the particle at a point on the boundary is described by its position vector and instantaneous velocity. Panel a shows the velocity decomposed into a radial-looking component and a tangential control term, labeled with an angle-dependent input. Panel b simplifies this to the same point and velocity without explicitly showing the tangential input, emphasizing the local geometric relation between motion and the boundary.\n\nThe bottom row appears to show the corresponding time-reversed or backward-in-time description. The position is written as a reversed trajectory term, and the velocity arrow points in the opposite direction compared with the top row. Panel c again includes the angular control term, now evaluated at reversed time, while panel d omits it as in the top-right panel.\n\nOverall, the figure illustrates a forward-versus-reversed trajectory construction near a rough boundary, highlighting how velocity and tangential control transform under time reversal.",
